  "description": "When the daemon that runs for good checks the disks' mounts, runs a pass, and how long it sleeps. A check is due once check_due_ns has come. A pass is due for each reason that holds, in this order: start (no pass since it started, first), reload (the configuration was read again, reloaded), gone (a disk went missing), back (a disk came back), events (a group ripened that someone other than Atoll made: ripe_origins holds anything but atoll), due (pass_due_ns, the last pass's next_due, has come), rescan (rescan_every_ns has gone by since last_pass_end_ns, and now is inside the window, in timezone). wake_ns is the earliest of: the next check, pass_due_ns, group_due_ns (when a waiting group ripens), and the next rescan, the first time inside the window at or after last_pass_end_ns + rescan_every_ns; never before now.",
